 "abs_ml": "In the application layer, a graph temporal network detected branch outages with an AUROC of 0.959 and an average precision of 0.243, above graph-only and time-only models, and GTN-based risk ranking reduced maintenance cost by 25.2% relative to time-based maintenance; PPO fine-tuning did not improve on this greedy policy.",
 "concl_ppo": "Ranking maintenance work by GTN failure risk lowered the episode cost by 25.2% against time-based maintenance with fewer than half of the crew dispatches, whereas PPO fine-tuning did not improve on that greedy rule within the training budget, so the learning-based allocation remains an open question rather than a result."
